# Axiom Project Rules — Auto-loaded by Cursor/Claude Code

## ⚠️ CRITICAL: Quirk & Debt Tracking Policy (AGENTS.md §0.5c)

When you encounter "quirk", "hack", "workaround", "fixme", "xxx", "nolint" in source code comments:

1. **NEVER remove or "fix" structured QUIRK markers** — they are formal tracking, NOT theater.
2. **Structured format ONLY**: `QUIRK(DEBT#xxx)` or `# axiom:quirk(DEBT#xxx)` is the ONLY allowed form.
3. **Bare euphemisms are THEATER**: Standalone `# hack`, `# workaround` without DEBT# ID = §0.9 violation.
4. **Double-binding required**: `QUIRK(DEBT#xxx)` MUST have corresponding `{.axiomDebt: "DEBT#xxx", kind: "quirk".}` pragma.

## Quick Decision Tree (for agents)

```
[ "quirk" / "hack" / "workaround" detected ]
  │
  ├─→ [ Has DEBT#xxx ID? ] ──NO──→ ❌ THEATER (blocked by architecture_invariants.nim)
  │        │
  │       YES
  │        │
  ├─→ [ Has {.axiomDebt.} pragma? ] ──NO──→ Add pragma first
  │        │
  │       YES
  │        │
  └─→ ✅ VALID SPEC (do NOT modify/remove)
```

## Mandatory Reading Before Modifying Gate Code

- Read AGENTS.md §0.9 (Theater Prohibition) before touching any gate runner
- Read AGENTS.md §0.5c (Debt/Quirk Spec) before modifying debt/quirk markers
- Check `data/debt_registry.json` before investigating suspected theater (0-token skip if entry exists)

